WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.850
With a strong cast and compelling storylines,
it's no wonder why "NCIS" has managed to become

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.020
one of the longest-running scripted series
in television history.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:14.720
The CBS megahit just wrapped up its 18th season,
and the series shows no signs of slowing down

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.720
any time soon.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.480
There will be plenty more crimes that require
solving for at least a bit longer, as the

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.369
network has already picked up the police procedural
for Season 19.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:27.380
But just because the show is coming back doesn't
mean that there aren't going to be some major

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.999
shake-ups along the way.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:32.900
The main cast members tend to stick around
for a while, with actors like Mark Harmon

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.230
and Sean Murray being there from the beginning.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.950
However, other actors have jumped ship over
the course of the show's long run, with their

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.930
characters moving on with their lives to do
something else beyond investigating crimes

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.690
-- and that appears to be what's transpiring
with Emily Wickersham, who's played fan-favorite

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.500
character Eleanor Bishop since Season 11.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.010
The Season 18 finale saw Eleanor undertake
a secret mission, but it was unclear to some

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.820
fans whether she would return or if this was
the end.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.910
The actress took to Instagram to confirm her
departure from the series, writing,

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.780
"Hangin this hat and jacket up.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.649
What a great ride it's been."

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:07.340
"It's awesome.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.640
It's been -- it's been really wonderful and
fun."

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.460
She genuinely seems to have enjoyed her time
on "NCIS," and there doesn't appear to be

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.600
any bad blood between her and any other cast
members.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.259
In other words, this doesn't seem to be the
kind of falling out that's alleged to occur

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:23.210
at the time of Pauley Perrette's exit from
the series.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.359
Given the fact Eleanor tells Nick Torres she
won't be back for a long time, it doesn't

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:30.789
seem likely that Bishop will be coming back
for any cameos anytime soon.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:34.240
With that unfortunate news in mind, here's
everything you need to know about why Emily

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.580
Wickersham is leaving "NCIS."

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:41.899
The actress announced her departure from the
series with an Instagram post on May 26, 2021.

00:01:41.899 --> 00:01:45.530
Throughout Wickersham's lengthy comments on
the matter, she doesn't mention anything about

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.649
why she chose to leave after Season 18 of
"NCIS."

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:52.639
The most likely explanation is that she merely
wanted to pursue other opportunities after

00:01:52.639 --> 00:01:56.840
playing the same character across eight seasons
and 172 episodes.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.490
"I mean if we worked, like, regular 9-to-5
jobs, things could be different."

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:05.759
Being free from the rigors of a network show's
shooting schedule would give her flexibility

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:10.149
in choosing other jobs, or even just taking
a break for a while and enjoying her hard-earned

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:11.149
success.

00:02:11.149 --> 00:02:14.540
But what's most important for fans of "NCIS"
is that it appears as though she's leaving

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.760
on good terms with everyone she worked with
over the last decade.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.760
"They're loose.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.440
Like the whole cast and crew is, like, loosey-goosey,
which makes for such a nice work environment.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.519
It really does."

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:24.730
As she mentions on Instagram,

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:29.090
"I've been lucky enough to be a part of a
show where I got to show up and act and laugh

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.940
and learn with wonderful people.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.319
A moment in time I surely won't forget.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.689
Thank you CBS and NCIS for including me in
a part of television history."

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:42.140
As you go down her post, you can see a slew
of comments from her many followers have already

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.310
come in, including one from the official CBS
Instagram account, which posted,

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.569
"Thanks for making history with us."

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:52.650
Wickersham's co-stars, including Maria Bello
and Brian Dietzen, also use their accounts

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.379
to express their pleasure of getting to work
with her for so many years.

00:02:56.379 --> 00:03:00.079
Wickersham's now free to pursue whatever projects
interest her the most from here on out.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:03.680
While it's still unclear where she'll end
up, bright things are inevitably in-store

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.450
for the talented actress.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.111
Wickersham's co-stars aren't the only ones
sad we won't see any more of Ellie Bishop

00:03:09.111 --> 00:03:11.349
eating snacks while putting clues together.

00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:16.290
"NCIS" fans took to Twitter in droves to express
their sadness at the Season 18 finale spelling

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.700
the end of Ellie -- as well as the much-loved
relationship between Ellie and Nick.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.180
Ellie Bishop served as an inspiration to plenty
of viewers, including one user who raved about

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.790
both her favorite character, and the talented
actor who plays her, writing,

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.400
"Maybe some people will never understand why
I'm so devastated but I'm 31 years old, I

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.610
grew up with #NCIS but I just connected with
ONE FEMALE CHARACTER!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.950
Emily Wickersham played Ellie Bishop, a powerful,
talented, persevering and empowered woman!"

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.959
Others talked about how Ellie had impacted
their lives beyond the small screen, influencing

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.030
the real world in a very real way.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.030
One person wrote,

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:53.860
"Thank you @EmilyWickersham for creating such
an amazing character — one that inspired

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.680
me to pursue a career in intelligence myself.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.079
Fans will miss you, but I think I speak for
all of us when I say there's only one Ellie

00:04:01.079 --> 00:04:02.079
Bishop."

